ts":-8.66},{"band":"60\u201365%","n":36,"pred":0.618,"hit":0.556,"units":2.64},{"band":"65\u2013100%","n":47,"pred":0.771,"hit":0.489,"units":-3.51}],"calibration_fit":{"completions":{"n":42,"brier_sim":0.245,"brier_market":0.2552,"best_w":1.0,"brier_best":0.245},"pass_td":{"n":42,"brier_sim":0.2478,"brier_market":0.2535,"best_w":1.0,"brier_best":0.2478},"pass_yds":{"n":42,"brier_sim":0.256,"brier_market":0.2503,"best_w":0.0,"brier_best":0.2503},"rec_yds":{"n":252,"brier_sim":0.2645,"brier_market":0.2502,"best_w":0.0,"brier_best":0.2502},"receptions":{"n":252,"brier_sim":0.2465,"brier_market":0.2498,"best_w":0.8,"brier_best":0.2461},"rush_yds":{"n":122,"brier_sim":0.2713,"brier_market":0.2506,"best_w":0.0,"brier_best":0.2506},"ALL":{"n":752,"brier_sim":0.2571,"brier_market":0.2506,"best_w":0.1,"brier_best":0.2505}},"factors":[{"factor":"OL/DL line grades (trench multipliers)","verdict":"KEEP \u2014 weight frozen, do not raise","numbers":"Brier on 438 lined player stats: base 0.2812, grades off 0.2812, half 0.2816, doubled 0.2826. Off helped rush attempts (0.2453 \u2192 0.2366, n=33) and hurt receptions (0.2687 \u2192 0.2706, n=142). Doubling was worse in all 6 markets.","why":"Net effect is zero within noise on one week. Doubling is clearly worse, so the trench weight stays at 15% of efficiency and is not raised. Run-game trench stays on watch: if rush attempts improve again with it off next week, it gets cut."},{"factor":"Raw sim probability vs the market","verdict":"REWEIGHT by market","numbers":"Brier on priced board lines: sim 0.2587 vs no-vig market 0.2519. By market \u2014 receptions sim 0.2461 vs market 0.2515 (sim better); rush yds 0.29 vs 0.25; rec yds 0.2561 vs 0.25; pass yds 0.2565 vs 0.2503.","why":"Each market now blends the sim toward the no-vig price with a learned weight (shrunk toward 50/50 so one week can't swing it): completions 0.54, pass_att 0.54, pass_td 0.59, pass_yds 0.41, rec_yds 0.33, receptions 0.72, rush_att 0.5, rush_rec_yds 0.3, rush_yds 0.3."},{"factor":"Over side","verdict":"PENALIZE overs by 3.2 pts","numbers":"Board overs went 81-117 (40.9%, -26.87u); unders 86-73 (54.1%, 21.95u). Week 9 overs were also over-predicted (54.6% sim vs 50.0% actual, 212 bets).","why":"Two straight weeks of overs landing under the sim. Overs now give back half the measured gap, capped at 4 points."},{"factor":"Blitz % (FTN n_blitzers, QB vs-blitz splits)","verdict":"ZERO \u2014 wired in, weight 0","numbers":"Week 10 sim backtest (13 games, 438 lined stats, 3 seeds x 4,000 draws): overall Brier base 0.2817 vs blitz-only 0.2821; QB pass yds 0.2864 \u2192 0.2852 (MAE 83.356 \u2192 83.117); completions 0.3085 \u2192 0.3091; rec yds 0.2901 \u2192 0.2911. Out-of-sample check on 175 QB games (2026 weeks 4\u201311, rates from earlier weeks only): the QB's blitz split made the forecast worse in every piece \u2014 comp% error +2.801%, YPA +1.157%, sack rate +5.751%. A defense's raw blitz rate does correlate with lower QB YPA vs his own baseline (r = -0.157), but the per-QB blitz splits point the wrong way too often.","why":"Wired end to end: every defense now carries its 2026 blitz rate and every QB with 40+ dropbacks carries his vs-blitz comp/YPA/sack split, in both the Python engine and the in-app sim. The evidence says the QB blitz splits add noise, so the weight is 0 (learning.json sim_factors.weights.blitz). It's re-tested each review and turns back on if it starts beating the base."},{"factor":"Defensive pressure vs QB under pressure","verdict":"KEEP for YPA and sacks (QB split at 50%), ZERO for completions and scrambles","numbers":"Week 10 sim backtest: overall Brier base 0.2817 vs pressure-matchup 0.2823, both 0.2826, final setting 0.2821; QB pass yds 0.2864 \u2192 0.285 (final 0.2857, side hit 0.436 \u2192 0.474); completions 0.3085 \u2192 0.3092; QB rush yds 0.2714 \u2192 0.2734. Out-of-sample on 175 QB games: YPA error -0.08% with the QB's own split and -0.193% with league-average sensitivity; sack-rate error -0.12% / -0.242%; comp% got worse (+1.079%) and scrambles got worse (+0.263%). Defense pressure rate vs QB YPA residual r = -0.12; vs sack-rate residual r = 0.072.","why":"Each defense's 2026 pressure rate (PFR times_pressured \u00f7 dropbacks faced) above or below league shifts the QB's pressured share. The change is that extra share times the QB's 2025 pressured-minus-clean gap, blended 50/50 with the league gap, then capped: YPA \u00b10.30, sack rate \u00b11.2 pts. Comp% and scramble pieces are zeroed because they made forecasts worse. Effects are small \u2014 a few pass yards per QB \u2014 and inside seed noise on one sim week (\u00b10.001 Brier), so this stays on probation."}],"takeaways":["Bets of the Night went 2-0: +0.068u at published stakes (+2.260u at 1u each).","Parlays of the Night went 2-6: +0.024u staked (+0.28u at 1u each).","War Room Picks of the Week went 3-2: nick_notes Dohnte Meyers over 2.5 receptions (loss); professor Ja'Marr Chase under 8.5 receptions (win); actuary Stefon Diggs under 4.5 receptions (win); alpha Mike Gesicki under 2.5 receptions (loss); coordinator Stefon Diggs under 55.5 rec yds (win).","Full board: 170-171 (49.9%), -16.98u on 256 priced props. Sim average miss 13.35 vs 12.77 for the posted line.","Overs 100-100 (-12.87u); unders 70-71 (-4.11u).","Pooled over graded weeks, sim Brier 0.2571 vs no-vig market 0.2506. Markets where the sim beat the price: completions, pass_td, receptions."],"improvements":[{"what":"Learning loop refit","done":"Weights now completions 0.65, pass_att 0.54, pass_td 0.65, pass_yds 0.35, rec_yds 0.14, receptions 0.71, rush_att 0.5, rush_rec_yds 0.3, rush_yds 0.23; over penalty 2.5 pts."}],"gaps":["No pre-kick board capture for: IND@HOU.","9 board props were void because the player wasn't in the ESPN box score.","CLV is measured against the last pre-kick capture from our own runs, not a true closing print.","No chat-only picks or personal tickets were logged for this week (pwa/data/review-extras file absen